WEBVTT

00:06.548 --> 00:09.092
[theme music]

00:45.086 --> 00:47.172
[thunder roars]

00:57.432 --> 00:59.642
- [phone ringing]
- [Mi-jin] Here's the numbers.

00:59.726 --> 01:01.519
- Look at this chart.
- [man 1] Go to check the center now.

01:02.937 --> 01:04.564
Look over here. Look at this.

01:04.647 --> 01:07.108
The direction headed over towards Japan.

01:07.192 --> 01:09.569
- Come on, Director. It can't be.
- It's coming in too strong.

01:09.652 --> 01:12.113
It's heading down from the north.
The temperature's following.

01:12.197 --> 01:14.616
So it's heading down
towards the southeast here.

01:14.699 --> 01:16.201
[Mi-jin] Is that what
the data says right now?

01:17.368 --> 01:18.495
[man 2] Wait a second.

01:19.704 --> 01:21.081
- No.
- Look.

01:21.164 --> 01:23.583
Hey, hey, hey. The current data.

01:24.209 --> 01:25.376
It's flowing this way.

01:25.460 --> 01:28.338
Okay, and this one's… Okay, so it's there.

01:28.421 --> 01:30.048
[wind blowing]

01:31.966 --> 01:33.676
[machine humming]

01:33.760 --> 01:35.553
[siren wailing]

01:43.520 --> 01:45.522
[suspenseful music]

01:47.148 --> 01:49.442
TYPHOON RICKY CONTINUES TO
CAUSE DAMAGE IN VARIOUS LOCATIONS

01:49.526 --> 01:51.152
- [Bong-chan groans]
- [Young-gil] Yes, I understand.

01:51.236 --> 01:52.904
- Sir.
- Ah!

01:54.614 --> 01:58.535
Yes. Ah! Do the… do the…
the rainfall forecast again.

01:58.618 --> 02:00.703
- [Young-gil] Yeah, right.
- Yeah? Yes?

02:00.787 --> 02:03.706
[phones ringing]

02:06.960 --> 02:09.003
- Hey, could I have you look at this?
- Of course.

02:09.087 --> 02:10.088
Great.

02:11.548 --> 02:13.550
- Okay.
- [phone clacks]

02:13.633 --> 02:15.051
[phone ringing]

02:15.135 --> 02:17.595
Yes, Team One here. Yes.

02:24.519 --> 02:27.230
- [leaves rustle]
- [wind blows]

02:30.108 --> 02:34.028
[reporter] Yesterday night, Typhoon Ricky
swept through the Korean Peninsula,

02:34.112 --> 02:35.905
wreaking havoc on the nation.

02:35.989 --> 02:39.742
Winds reached 30m per second,
resulting in a 120 injured or dead,

02:39.826 --> 02:43.413
causing 80 billion won in damages
across the Korean Peninsula.

02:43.496 --> 02:48.126
The downpour last night also caused
flooding and damage in many areas.

02:48.209 --> 02:50.044
- Today at dawn in Yangcheon-gu, Seoul…
- Whoa!

02:50.128 --> 02:52.755
- …firefighters are already…
- Looks like this time the KMA was right.

02:52.839 --> 02:53.923
…after it became flooded.

02:54.007 --> 02:55.842
Then I guess Ha-kyung
won't get so much hate.

02:55.925 --> 02:57.969
- …underground shops and apartment…
- [crunches]

02:58.052 --> 02:59.804
Yes, yes, yes, that's right.

03:00.346 --> 03:04.684
Yes, the typhoon followed
our estimated path fairly closely.

03:05.268 --> 03:08.021
[Ha-kyung] We live with many
different scenarios.

03:08.104 --> 03:10.231
…rainfall also, yes. Uh-huh.

03:11.316 --> 03:12.901
[giggles]
Yes, pretty much. Thanks.

03:12.984 --> 03:14.360
Yes. Yes.

03:15.904 --> 03:19.198
TYPHOON'S PREDICTED PATH CLOSELY MATCHES
WITH THE FORECAST OF THE KMA

03:22.327 --> 03:25.997
[Ha-kyung] Sometimes, the scenario
we prepared for is accurate.

03:28.499 --> 03:30.501
[light music]

03:33.463 --> 03:35.298
I'm getting up to use the bathroom.

03:42.013 --> 03:44.724
Why did we bring this guy with us anyway?

03:45.808 --> 03:47.268
This was the best course of action.

03:50.480 --> 03:55.485
I want to help fix Si-woo's relationship
with him, as well as ours.

03:58.154 --> 04:00.156
[emotional music]

04:06.120 --> 04:07.080
[Si-woo] Some things…

04:07.705 --> 04:09.749
are impossible in this life.

04:10.500 --> 04:13.378
Like a person can never stop
a typhoon coming in,

04:13.461 --> 04:15.755
my dad isn't something you can change.

04:16.798 --> 04:20.134
That man will never
put in the work to change.

04:22.762 --> 04:24.764
I need to keep looking out for myself.

04:25.348 --> 04:27.267
I know you'll do the same thing too.

04:32.605 --> 04:33.523
Forgive me.

04:34.816 --> 04:36.276
I can't be what you want.

04:39.862 --> 04:40.780
So let's…

04:43.157 --> 04:44.367
end it.

04:50.248 --> 04:52.250
[emotional music]

04:55.795 --> 04:58.881
[Ha-kyung] Sometimes,
the scenario you expected is wrong,

04:59.716 --> 05:02.844
and the actuality causes a catastrophe.

05:07.724 --> 05:09.309
So you came here to negotiate?

05:10.893 --> 05:11.728
I did.

05:17.567 --> 05:18.443
Yu-jin…

05:33.249 --> 05:36.586
[Ha-kyung] The important thing
is that life goes on

05:36.669 --> 05:39.922
whether your scenario was right or wrong.

05:40.006 --> 05:43.259
You heard typhoon 15's
also coming our way, huh?

05:44.010 --> 05:45.887
Uh, judging from the chart…

05:45.970 --> 05:47.472
- Eight hours? Uh-huh?
- [Dong-han] Yes.

05:47.555 --> 05:50.600
In eight hours, it'll be on top
of the Korean Peninsula.

05:50.683 --> 05:53.102
So you don't have
to come back up to Seoul.

05:53.186 --> 05:54.729
Just stay there and track the new one.

05:54.812 --> 05:55.897
Huh?

05:56.731 --> 05:58.649
Yeah, of course there. Where else?

05:59.317 --> 06:01.611
The typhoon center,
get over there right now.

06:02.195 --> 06:05.531
- [Bong-chan] Go on, hurry.
- [Ha-kyung] What? Right now?

06:06.365 --> 06:08.034
- Sir, no. I still got to be--
- [line beeps]

06:12.246 --> 06:14.582
[somber music]

06:14.665 --> 06:16.334
[Ha-kyung] So we have to prepare…

06:17.210 --> 06:20.880
for the next scenario
and the next after that.

06:20.963 --> 06:22.632
[sighs]

06:22.715 --> 06:24.092
[thunder roars]

06:27.178 --> 06:33.184
EPISODE 13
SCENARIO 1, 2, 3

06:33.267 --> 06:35.686
- [breathes deeply]
- [approaching footsteps]

06:43.111 --> 06:43.986
[sighs]

06:45.571 --> 06:46.989
[chuckles]

06:52.120 --> 06:55.623
- So when did you find out?
- [sighs, clears throat]

06:55.706 --> 06:56.916
I've known a while.

06:57.500 --> 06:58.668
[yawns]

07:00.128 --> 07:00.962
Hmm?

07:01.045 --> 07:03.381
[playful music]

07:06.175 --> 07:07.969
[awkward chuckle]

07:08.052 --> 07:11.264
- [gasps]
- Whoa! That quickly? Really?

07:12.140 --> 07:13.975
What about you? When did you know?

07:14.058 --> 07:17.437
I had a feeling
for quite a long time, really.

07:17.520 --> 07:18.855
[giggles]

07:22.608 --> 07:23.443
[sneezes]

07:24.652 --> 07:26.362
[Myung-ju] It sounds like you got a cold.

07:26.446 --> 07:27.405
Yeah.

07:27.488 --> 07:30.241
We will now call to order
our meeting for May 10th.

07:30.324 --> 07:31.451
Okay, satellite--
[sneezes]

07:32.994 --> 07:34.996
[Ha-kyung] I apol… I apologize.

07:35.079 --> 07:36.956
Um, if you, uh…

07:37.039 --> 07:38.416
Thank… thank you very much.

07:39.208 --> 07:41.127
[Ha-kyung sniffles]

07:43.171 --> 07:46.048
- [giggling]
- Oh, my God. No, really. I've got chills.

07:46.132 --> 07:48.885
That's so long ago. Oh, my God!

07:50.011 --> 07:51.304
So how'd you know, then?

07:52.054 --> 07:53.473
Way later than you.

07:54.098 --> 07:55.475
Oh, wait. You know.

07:57.727 --> 07:59.729
[keyboards clacking]

08:01.814 --> 08:02.815
[Si-woo] Oh.

08:02.899 --> 08:05.359
[keyboards clacking]

08:09.697 --> 08:10.531
[chuckles]

08:11.240 --> 08:13.743
[keyboards clacking]

08:16.871 --> 08:18.789
[all laughing]

08:18.873 --> 08:22.001
Yeah, that one was very unsubtle.
[chuckles]

08:22.084 --> 08:25.796
I mean, they were so obvious that
it was hard to pretend not to notice.

08:25.880 --> 08:26.714
[gasps]

08:30.760 --> 08:33.137
Stop messing around, okay, Forecaster?

08:33.721 --> 08:34.722
Yes, ma'am.

08:34.805 --> 08:37.099
[Myung-ju] Oh, they just
wouldn't give it a rest.

08:37.183 --> 08:39.018
[giggling]

08:39.769 --> 08:42.480
So, then, uh, what now from now on?

08:43.064 --> 08:45.066
What do you think? We reveal nothing.

08:45.566 --> 08:49.028
We just keep quiet like we were doing.
Pretend not to know.

08:51.572 --> 08:54.659
- [Dong-han] Pretend not to know what?
- [Soo-jin coughs, clears throat]

08:54.742 --> 08:57.370
- Huh?
- What? What?

08:57.870 --> 08:59.872
I show up, and now you're all quiet?

08:59.956 --> 09:01.749
[chuckles]
No, it's nothing, really.

09:03.376 --> 09:05.503
[chuckling]

09:16.305 --> 09:18.224
Forecaster Um knows, right?

09:18.307 --> 09:20.768
Of course, he does.
He went on that retreat.

09:20.851 --> 09:22.853
How oblivious would he
have to be not to know it?

09:22.937 --> 09:24.313
[chuckles]

09:24.397 --> 09:25.439
[Myung-ju] "Oblivious"?

09:25.523 --> 09:26.399
[Myung-ju laughs]

09:27.108 --> 09:28.192
Me, right?

09:28.693 --> 09:29.610
Huh?

09:29.694 --> 09:30.695
Mm-mm.

09:30.778 --> 09:32.154
Uh, no. Not you. Not you.

09:33.531 --> 09:36.617
[sighs]
Wow, you guys hear it all.

09:37.159 --> 09:39.412
It's true. My wife, she wants a divorce.

09:40.288 --> 09:42.415
[quirky music]

09:48.296 --> 09:51.132
How on earth did you find out?
[clicks tongue]

09:54.010 --> 09:57.513
[Myung-han] Sir, I only have 6,000 won.

09:58.222 --> 10:00.474
Could you please
just take me to the airport?

10:00.558 --> 10:02.518
Please? Hey, please!

10:02.602 --> 10:05.146
Oh, hey! Hey!

10:05.229 --> 10:06.397
Damn it.

10:09.066 --> 10:11.027
Uh, for heaven's sake.

10:14.071 --> 10:16.115
[Myung-han sighs]
Shit! Damn it.

10:17.742 --> 10:19.660
[blows air]

10:20.953 --> 10:22.121
[sighs]

10:26.208 --> 10:27.543
Hey, Director Lady.

10:28.794 --> 10:30.254
Let me ask you something.

10:32.715 --> 10:35.885
You knew perfectly well that
Si-woo didn't want to see me there,

10:35.968 --> 10:38.471
so why are we in this town?

10:40.640 --> 10:41.974
I also have a question.

10:42.558 --> 10:44.060
[Ha-kyung] Your son's injured.

10:44.143 --> 10:45.811
So how come the money's all you want?

10:46.562 --> 10:47.855
[tongue clicks]

10:47.938 --> 10:50.566
In this world, you gotta watch your nose.

10:50.650 --> 10:52.276
Let your guard down, they'll cut it off.

10:52.360 --> 10:54.320
You let people slide, and they'll get you.

10:54.403 --> 10:56.530
I'm his father.
One of us should keep alert

10:56.614 --> 10:58.783
and get what's ours from this.

11:00.159 --> 11:01.869
So what's the problem?

11:02.912 --> 11:06.040
[Ha-kyung] There are
many different fathers in this world.

11:08.042 --> 11:10.461
[emotional music]

11:12.088 --> 11:15.132
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

11:16.258 --> 11:17.635
[sighs]

11:31.524 --> 11:33.526
[laughs]

11:36.987 --> 11:38.406
[sucks teeth]

11:38.489 --> 11:41.033
[Ha-kyung] There are fathers
who try their best,

11:41.117 --> 11:44.412
yet always feel they could do better
for their children.

11:45.621 --> 11:49.667
There are also those irresponsible fathers

11:50.459 --> 11:52.837
who run away, leaving young kids alone.

11:53.754 --> 11:54.672
And there are fathers

11:54.755 --> 11:58.008
who are utterly shameless
and selfish with their children.

12:00.678 --> 12:02.096
[Myung-han] Damn it.

12:02.179 --> 12:03.389
Damn it!

12:04.098 --> 12:05.599
I should never have followed you.

12:06.851 --> 12:08.352
[lighter ignites]

12:14.316 --> 12:15.943
You'll have to go to Seoul alone.

12:18.654 --> 12:19.572
[bag thuds]

12:35.546 --> 12:36.589
[car door closes]

12:45.055 --> 12:47.266
[emotional music]

12:48.434 --> 12:50.144
[vehicle approaching]

12:56.567 --> 12:57.401
[car door opens]

13:08.746 --> 13:11.415
Get in. I'll take you to your mom's house.

13:14.627 --> 13:17.296
I really have to talk to you.
Get in the car.

13:17.379 --> 13:21.175
- [sighs]
- [bus approaching]

13:22.927 --> 13:26.013
- [brakes squealing]
- [bus doors open]

13:30.601 --> 13:31.602
[bus doors close]

13:33.187 --> 13:35.314
[engine revs]

13:45.449 --> 13:48.160
[gloomy music]

14:02.800 --> 14:05.427
[birds squawking]

14:18.691 --> 14:21.902
Why are they sending a director
from the main office all the way here?

14:22.444 --> 14:23.821
She doesn't look like
she'll be a lot of help.

14:25.573 --> 14:27.449
If you say so, Director General, I will.

14:27.992 --> 14:29.577
- Yes, sir. I know.
- [glasses clack]

14:33.163 --> 14:35.249
Right now, Elisha's
central pressure is 985,

14:35.332 --> 14:37.585
max wind speed
at the center, 27 per second.

14:37.668 --> 14:40.921
It's moving north from the sea
250km south of Jeju.

14:41.005 --> 14:42.006
At this size and speed,

14:42.089 --> 14:44.925
it'll make landfall
on the south coast. And you?

14:45.009 --> 14:46.802
I'll observe the heading.

14:46.886 --> 14:49.179
You stick to synoptic weather observation.

14:49.972 --> 14:50.931
Understood?

14:51.557 --> 14:52.516
Yes, of course.

14:52.600 --> 14:54.727
SYNOPTIC WEATHER OBSERVATION: OBSERVATIONS
MADE AT A SPECIFIC TIME AT ALL STATIONS

14:54.810 --> 14:56.228
How's Forecaster Lee?

14:57.271 --> 14:58.939
Uh, they finished treating him
for the burn.

14:59.023 --> 15:01.108
But with the eye,
they'll have to watch what happens.

15:01.191 --> 15:03.068
- [paper rustles]
- Is that so?

15:05.571 --> 15:09.116
Someone got seriously hurt,
and you don't seem to care, huh?

15:09.199 --> 15:11.702
[tense music]

15:14.580 --> 15:18.959
Are you saying your teammate got wounded
because of me?

15:20.711 --> 15:22.504
No, I'm saying

15:22.588 --> 15:26.634
you should at least try to show
some more care and concern for him.

15:26.717 --> 15:27.927
[scoffs]

15:30.846 --> 15:31.972
[Mi-jin] Director Jin.

15:32.765 --> 15:36.143
You've worked at Headquarters
your whole career, right?

15:36.226 --> 15:37.227
Yes. So what?

15:40.105 --> 15:41.482
[Mi-jin] Do you know what this is?

15:43.651 --> 15:46.362
Baengnokdam, an accident, at the AWS.

15:46.445 --> 15:47.780
I slipped and tore it open.

15:51.408 --> 15:52.826
Assistant Director Park there,

15:52.910 --> 15:55.120
the hearing in his left ear
comes and goes.

15:55.204 --> 15:56.580
He went out on the field
during a rainstorm

15:56.664 --> 15:57.665
and was hit by a street sign.

15:59.959 --> 16:04.254
Mr. Yang here had his car overturned
when he went to observe the wind fields.

16:06.882 --> 16:09.635
Everyone here who's been doing this
longer than ten years

16:09.718 --> 16:11.762
could tell you a similar situation.

16:11.845 --> 16:13.764
I'm sorry that Forecaster Lee got hurt.

16:13.847 --> 16:16.266
But around here, it happens to all of us.

16:17.017 --> 16:19.019
Understand me, Director?

16:21.689 --> 16:22.523
Yes.

16:23.190 --> 16:24.024
[staff] Director?

16:26.026 --> 16:28.153
When they say
director around here, it's me.

16:28.237 --> 16:29.738
- [staff] Could you?
- Mm-hmm.

16:34.326 --> 16:35.494
[sighs]

16:40.499 --> 16:41.542
[breathes deeply]

16:50.050 --> 16:51.051
[Mi-jin] What?

16:51.969 --> 16:53.679
Why are you here and not in the hospital?

16:55.472 --> 16:58.058
Turns out it wasn't as bad
as they expected.

16:58.142 --> 17:00.310
And I've always healed pretty quickly.

17:00.394 --> 17:01.770
I thought you hurt your eye too.

17:01.854 --> 17:04.857
They, uh, have to watch it
for three days, that's all.

17:04.940 --> 17:06.775
So far, no problems with it.

17:11.155 --> 17:12.823
Did you hear that, Director?

17:27.212 --> 17:28.464
We need to talk.

17:32.468 --> 17:34.762
[gloomy music]

17:48.859 --> 17:51.111
[Hyang-rae] No. No more. Enough.

17:51.779 --> 17:53.655
Just be a decent man for once and sign it.

17:53.739 --> 17:57.201
Sign the paper and we can both go on
and move on with our lives.

17:57.910 --> 18:00.037
It's what's best for everyone, yeah?

18:06.043 --> 18:07.878
[sighs]

18:09.046 --> 18:10.214
[sniffles]

18:13.592 --> 18:15.010
[message alert tone]

18:16.553 --> 18:19.056
- [mouse clicks]
- [Tae-kyung] How's this character?

18:19.139 --> 18:21.308
- [computer beeps]
- [chuckles]

18:21.391 --> 18:23.310
JIN TAE-KYUNG

18:24.686 --> 18:25.646
[chuckles]

18:25.729 --> 18:26.563
[mouse clicks]

18:32.277 --> 18:33.862
- [Seok-ho] Cute.
- [computer chimes]

18:37.074 --> 18:39.409
SAVE

18:39.493 --> 18:42.121
- [mouse clicking]
- [giggles]

18:42.204 --> 18:45.332
[mouse clicking]

18:48.627 --> 18:51.755
- So the typhoon post is done?
- Oh, uh… No.

18:54.174 --> 18:56.593
- The post is going up now.
- [Myung-ju] Okay.

18:57.261 --> 19:01.056
- [mouse clicking]
- [keyboard clacking]

19:01.140 --> 19:02.808
[Seok-ho] See you after work.

19:09.606 --> 19:12.151
TYPHOON REPORT
UPLOADING

19:12.985 --> 19:14.236
[message alert tone]

19:14.319 --> 19:15.863
[Mi-jin-jin] Soo-jin, could you
come out a second?

19:20.075 --> 19:21.201
ASSISTANT DIRECTOR PARK SUNG-JIN

19:22.953 --> 19:24.079
[Soo-jin] Okay.

19:25.622 --> 19:27.499
I'm running over to the Policy Office.

19:27.583 --> 19:28.542
[Myung-ju] Okay.

19:30.210 --> 19:32.045
- [papers rustling]
- [phone buzzes]

19:32.129 --> 19:33.255
GYEOL'S HOMEROOM TEACHER

19:33.338 --> 19:34.256
[Myung-ju] Oh.

19:34.339 --> 19:37.176
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

19:38.677 --> 19:40.470
Hello. Yes. How are you?

19:41.263 --> 19:43.724
Ah, whoa! He did that? Uh…

19:44.308 --> 19:47.352
Uh, yes. Um… He does that.

19:47.936 --> 19:48.896
Oh.

19:49.855 --> 19:51.273
Yes. Yes, of course.

19:52.191 --> 19:55.485
TYPHOON REPORT
UPLOADING

19:55.569 --> 19:57.196
Go to the hospital.

19:57.779 --> 19:59.448
[Si-woo] I've already been discharged.

19:59.531 --> 20:02.075
I'm totally good to work right now.

20:04.828 --> 20:06.622
You do whatever you wanna do, huh?

20:08.832 --> 20:10.459
- [rain pouring]
- [Si-woo] So let's…

20:11.126 --> 20:12.127
end it.

20:18.091 --> 20:20.344
Just say whatever you want, and that's it?

20:20.928 --> 20:22.804
Okay. Well, you said your part.

20:23.680 --> 20:24.890
But I haven't responded.

20:26.099 --> 20:27.309
So you can just hang on.

20:29.186 --> 20:30.187
[approaching footsteps]

20:30.270 --> 20:32.773
[panting]
Director Jin. You need to come in here.

20:38.153 --> 20:41.323
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION
NATIONAL TYPHOON CENTER

20:42.199 --> 20:43.408
What's going on?

20:43.992 --> 20:45.244
That's what I wanted to know.

20:46.495 --> 20:47.663
What's going on?

20:47.746 --> 20:49.623
[funky music]

20:51.041 --> 20:53.502
Hey, what did you post for the report?

20:53.585 --> 20:55.963
Report? What? Which one?

21:05.931 --> 21:07.516
[Dong-han] Hold it. What?

21:08.100 --> 21:09.851
Why is the report a penguin?

21:12.271 --> 21:13.146
[gasps]

21:14.147 --> 21:15.148
[Myung-ju] Mr. Shin.

21:15.232 --> 21:16.566
Did you upload that?

21:25.534 --> 21:26.868
Go on! Delete it!

21:28.662 --> 21:30.455
Yes… Yes.

21:30.539 --> 21:31.456
[thuds]

21:32.833 --> 21:34.584
[sighs]
Jeez.

21:36.044 --> 21:37.337
TYPHOON REPORT

21:37.421 --> 21:38.672
[Mi-jin sighs]

21:38.755 --> 21:41.008
The typhoon's making landfall,
and this is what they post?

21:41.550 --> 21:43.093
Is this how your department runs?

21:43.176 --> 21:46.430
Not even our day-one hires
would have messed that up.

21:49.516 --> 21:50.475
Is it Mr. Shin?

21:55.439 --> 21:57.065
[phone vibrates]

22:00.277 --> 22:02.029
Yes, hello. What happened?

22:03.238 --> 22:04.448
[Dong-han] Mr. Shin…

22:05.365 --> 22:06.616
Um, well…

22:07.284 --> 22:09.369
he uploaded, uh, the wrong file.

22:09.453 --> 22:11.413
[Myung-ju sighs]
It's all my fault.

22:12.205 --> 22:13.665
I was distracted.

22:15.250 --> 22:16.376
[Dong-han] No.

22:16.460 --> 22:21.173
I don't know what the penguin's for
or why it's on a work computer.

22:21.923 --> 22:25.093
[Tae-kyung humming]

22:32.267 --> 22:34.186
Okay, Mr. Um, now really,

22:34.269 --> 22:37.105
have you forgotten
you're acting director when I'm gone?

22:38.774 --> 22:41.943
I know you're all happy
about the typhoon 14 analysis.

22:42.027 --> 22:43.361
Another one's almost here.

22:43.445 --> 22:45.655
[Dong-han] I'm sorry. I have no excuse.

22:45.739 --> 22:46.740
Oh, uh…

22:46.823 --> 22:48.617
Forgive him, Director. Uh…

22:49.201 --> 22:51.745
Forecaster Um's having
a hard time right now.

22:52.370 --> 22:55.123
His… wife's about to divorce him.

22:56.875 --> 22:58.168
Huh?

22:58.251 --> 23:00.921
I know it's all just so hard for him.

23:01.004 --> 23:02.756
[Myung-ju] I should
have paid more attention.

23:03.465 --> 23:05.092
It's entirely my fault, Director.

23:05.175 --> 23:06.635
- Why would you say that?
- I'm sorry.

23:06.718 --> 23:09.930
- What if it's on speaker?
- [Seok-ho] It's my fault, Director.

23:10.013 --> 23:11.181
- Seok-ho, what?
- [Myung-ju] Give me the phone!

23:11.264 --> 23:13.850
This terrible mistake
in the face of a typhoon is…

23:13.934 --> 23:17.521
Honestly, yes, well,
it's just so inexcusable to me.

23:17.604 --> 23:20.941
Yes, yes, all mine, all my fault.
I'll write a disciplinary report.

23:21.024 --> 23:22.609
- Huh?
- [Seok-ho] If the report's not enough,

23:22.692 --> 23:24.194
a dock of my pay would be appropriate.

23:24.277 --> 23:25.195
- Don't say that!
- What are you saying?

23:25.278 --> 23:27.447
- No, Director. It's my fault.
- Come on, man! Don't say that.

23:27.531 --> 23:28.907
- [Myung-ju] I should have checked.
- [Seok-ho] No. It's my fault.

23:28.990 --> 23:30.700
- No, please!
- I, I just…

23:30.784 --> 23:32.994
- It's not your fault.
- Mr. Um's on the verge of a divorce.

23:33.078 --> 23:34.955
- Assistant Director Oh--
- [Seok-ho] Everything's my fault.

23:35.038 --> 23:36.581
- I can't hear you speak.
- [overlapping chatter]

23:36.665 --> 23:40.168
Okay, one at a time.
I can't hear any of you!

23:45.799 --> 23:46.716
[Dong-jin] Yu-jin!

23:46.800 --> 23:47.801
[Dong-jin panting]

23:47.884 --> 23:50.303
- Don't run, don't run, you'll fall.
- Ki-jun is here.

23:51.429 --> 23:52.347
Really?

23:55.976 --> 23:58.103
[birds chirping]

24:01.523 --> 24:02.816
Why are you here?

24:03.525 --> 24:05.277
Well, I said I had to talk to you.

24:07.863 --> 24:08.905
[Yu-jin's mom gasps]

24:08.989 --> 24:11.241
- Oh, you're here.
- [Ki-jun] Here, allow me.

24:11.324 --> 24:12.701
Oh, thanks.

24:12.784 --> 24:14.786
[Yu-jin's mom] Yu-jin, take this
and go inside and eat.

24:14.870 --> 24:16.955
I'm gonna go and get things for dinner.

24:17.038 --> 24:18.748
Uh, no, it's all right.

24:18.832 --> 24:22.460
Ah, no. You came all the way here.
You need at least one good meal.

24:25.922 --> 24:27.716
- [sighs]
- Yu-jin.

24:33.722 --> 24:36.558
I don't know what the matter is,
but I do try to placate her.

24:37.225 --> 24:40.353
She's not usually wind up
so tight, you know, hmm?

24:40.437 --> 24:41.354
Sure.

24:43.398 --> 24:45.984
[gloomy music]

24:46.067 --> 24:47.861
[sucks teeth]

24:47.944 --> 24:49.446
She asked for a divorce.

24:50.030 --> 24:51.406
[Ha-kyung] Out of the blue?

24:54.284 --> 24:56.620
I wouldn't say that, no.

24:58.038 --> 24:59.581
So what did you tell her?

25:00.165 --> 25:01.249
Well, what could I say?

25:01.333 --> 25:02.792
You're just going to go along with it?

25:02.876 --> 25:05.170
[sighs]
She said that I should…

25:05.712 --> 25:06.963
to keep it simple.

25:07.589 --> 25:10.383
[Dong-han] I just made her life
very difficult.

25:10.467 --> 25:11.968
And if I try to hold on now,

25:12.552 --> 25:15.138
I'm afraid I'll make it even worse.

25:16.556 --> 25:18.308
You can't just roll over.

25:18.975 --> 25:20.977
How do I change her mind, though?

25:21.061 --> 25:23.230
You need a plan to persuade her
or whatever.

25:23.313 --> 25:24.397
Or just explain.

25:24.481 --> 25:25.565
Wait, how?

25:26.983 --> 25:28.735
You know, three scenarios.

25:36.368 --> 25:37.994
[Yu-jin] What did you come here for?

25:38.828 --> 25:40.622
To see you, of course.

25:41.248 --> 25:42.874
[Ki-jun] We can't end this way.

25:42.958 --> 25:44.501
I needed to do something.

25:45.085 --> 25:47.462
What will that be? What else is there?

25:53.051 --> 25:55.387
[bright music]

25:55.470 --> 25:57.722
- Oppa.
- I'm sorry, Yu-jin.

25:58.723 --> 26:01.226
Your oppa's sorry
he caused you pain and hurt you.

26:02.143 --> 26:03.311
He's sorry for everything.

26:03.395 --> 26:05.355
[sighs]
Why are you down there?

26:06.189 --> 26:08.233
- [Yu-jin] Get up.
- [moans]

26:10.402 --> 26:11.486
Okay, stand.

26:11.569 --> 26:13.446
Please let's go back
to Seoul together, Yu-jin.

26:13.530 --> 26:14.823
[sighs]

26:14.906 --> 26:16.074
Get off the ground.

26:16.157 --> 26:19.494
I will as long as you say
you'll come along.

26:19.577 --> 26:20.787
[sighs]

26:28.253 --> 26:29.629
- Come on, get up.
- Mm.

26:30.171 --> 26:31.214
Answer me.

26:31.298 --> 26:33.550
All right, fine! Whatever! Just get up.

26:33.633 --> 26:34.843
You… you mean it?

26:34.926 --> 26:36.886
We're going to go together?
You'll go with me?

26:36.970 --> 26:38.847
Uh-huh, yeah. Get off the grass.

26:38.930 --> 26:40.390
[Ki-jun grunts]

26:40.473 --> 26:41.558
[sighs]
Jeez.

26:41.641 --> 26:43.518
[chuckles]

26:51.026 --> 26:53.486
[gloomy music]

26:57.782 --> 27:01.411
[Seok-ho] I admit I made a mistake,
but I can't elaborate on why.

27:02.579 --> 27:06.207
I'm sorry. It's personal,
so I can't tell you.

27:09.461 --> 27:12.422
I think my husband is no longer focused.

27:14.132 --> 27:16.760
[Myung-ju] His Level Five
Civil Service Exam is coming up soon.

27:18.136 --> 27:19.804
And my mother-in-law says

27:19.888 --> 27:21.681
she couldn't take care
of the kids anymore.

27:21.765 --> 27:23.350
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

27:23.433 --> 27:25.101
[Dong-han] My wife asked me for a divorce.

27:30.231 --> 27:31.358
So let's…

27:33.610 --> 27:34.778
end it.

27:41.826 --> 27:44.287
What does the GDAPS show?

27:44.371 --> 27:46.373
GDAPS: GLOBAL DATA ASSIMILATION
AND PREDICTION SYSTEM

27:47.415 --> 27:50.460
The speed is increasing
'cause of the rising jet current.

27:50.543 --> 27:53.088
Vertical wind shear is over 50.

27:53.880 --> 27:54.964
Ah, okay.

28:16.319 --> 28:18.488
Did you figure out who sent that file?

28:19.447 --> 28:20.490
Yes, well…

28:20.573 --> 28:22.992
Just another day at Headquarters.
[sighs]

28:24.369 --> 28:27.247
You people over there sit
in your comfy situation room chairs

28:27.330 --> 28:29.999
clicking around all day, so you get weak.

28:32.794 --> 28:35.672
Haven't you ever made
an error like that, Director?

28:37.465 --> 28:41.052
I know that everyone
goes out in the field here,

28:41.136 --> 28:43.805
risking your lives
and getting hurt in the process.

28:43.888 --> 28:45.098
[Ha-kyung] I know.

28:45.181 --> 28:47.475
The situation room's no cake walk either.

28:50.770 --> 28:53.064
[tender music]

28:53.148 --> 28:55.400
[Ha-kyung] Someone's
about to get divorced.

28:57.068 --> 28:59.362
- Follow those from there to there.
- [phone vibrating]

28:59.446 --> 29:00.613
MOTHER-IN-LAW

29:01.865 --> 29:04.159
Yes, hello.
I'm-- I'm sorry, Mom. I'm working.

29:04.242 --> 29:06.327
One sec, please. Send this to me?

29:06.411 --> 29:07.328
Thanks, sorry.

29:08.329 --> 29:10.415
[Ha-kyung] Someone works
her hands to the bone,

29:10.498 --> 29:14.711
providing for her whole family
but never stops saying sorry.

29:14.794 --> 29:16.254
Yes, I'm sorry. Uh-huh.

29:20.175 --> 29:21.301
[sighs]

29:21.384 --> 29:24.179
[Ha-kyung] Someone has to watch
the seasons go by on the monitor.

29:24.262 --> 29:25.430
[phone clacks]

29:31.227 --> 29:33.396
[exhales heavily]
Okay. We upload…

29:33.480 --> 29:37.400
[Ha-kyung] Someone's youth is passing by
without a single real relationship.

29:41.237 --> 29:42.697
Are we competing, huh?

29:42.781 --> 29:45.992
Who here has had the worst time
working at the KMA?

29:46.075 --> 29:47.494
[sighs]
No.

29:47.577 --> 29:50.330
I'm saying typhoon center
or situation room,

29:50.413 --> 29:53.208
all of us are working so hard
to get it right here.

29:54.083 --> 29:56.669
So stop trying to so little divisions,

29:56.753 --> 29:59.547
comparing all that
is beneath you, Director.

30:08.264 --> 30:10.558
- Excuse me.
- [employee] Yes?

30:10.642 --> 30:13.394
- Get us the scenario analysis.
- [employee] Uh, okay.

30:13.478 --> 30:15.355
[papers rustle]

30:20.235 --> 30:21.736
[sighs]

30:23.196 --> 30:24.781
- [door lock beeps]
- [door opens]

30:27.659 --> 30:29.410
[door lock beeps]

30:30.537 --> 30:31.746
[sighs]

30:35.124 --> 30:37.377
What are you doing here at this hour?

30:37.460 --> 30:38.336
Uh…

30:40.296 --> 30:41.923
Give me a chance, Hyang-rae.

30:43.591 --> 30:44.801
[Dong-han] Just three months.

30:44.884 --> 30:48.263
Let's have a grace period.
Just 90 days, and then…

30:49.472 --> 30:50.557
What does that mean?

30:50.640 --> 30:54.602
Honestly, I… I don't…
I don't think that you're being fair.

30:54.686 --> 30:59.065
So for three months,
let's try and live together.

31:00.108 --> 31:03.027
And then I'll do anything you want, okay?

31:03.111 --> 31:06.906
Huh? If you say you want a divorce,
I'll let you do it.

31:06.990 --> 31:09.534
If you want me
to get out of Seoul, then I'll go.

31:10.994 --> 31:12.912
And what do you want from all that?

31:12.996 --> 31:14.205
It's just that…

31:14.956 --> 31:17.375
Even death row gives you some grace
at the end, huh?

31:17.959 --> 31:22.255
Can't you at least give me just…
just a shred longer, huh?

31:22.338 --> 31:25.216
You have to see I work so hard
for all of us for so long.

31:29.095 --> 31:30.805
Then why are you here and not at work?

31:32.432 --> 31:34.726
I'm on lunch. I ran here.

31:34.809 --> 31:37.562
Then you'll be late.
Go back to your office.

31:37.645 --> 31:39.939
- Oh, honey. Honey.
- Just go, okay?

31:41.441 --> 31:42.650
[sighs]

31:44.402 --> 31:46.613
[somber music]

31:54.579 --> 31:56.205
[door lock beeps]

32:12.347 --> 32:14.474
[somber music]

32:29.364 --> 32:30.490
- [sighs]
- [thuds]

32:42.919 --> 32:44.837
[phone vibrates]

32:46.297 --> 32:48.007
Hey, hey, Hyang-rae.

32:48.675 --> 32:50.093
[Hyang-rae] What's all this?

32:50.593 --> 32:51.678
Huh?

32:54.889 --> 32:56.391
[Dong-han] Oh, that.

32:56.975 --> 32:58.309
Typhoon's landing soon.

32:58.393 --> 33:01.187
Looks like very high winds,
so I put that in.

33:03.940 --> 33:04.983
Are you there?

33:06.818 --> 33:07.819
Hello, honey?

33:07.902 --> 33:10.196
[Hyang-rae] I just can't do three months.

33:11.447 --> 33:12.532
Oh…

33:13.908 --> 33:15.118
'kay.

33:15.201 --> 33:16.035
[Dong-han sighs]

33:17.620 --> 33:18.746
Two's okay.

33:20.540 --> 33:21.666
"Two"?

33:21.749 --> 33:24.335
Anything you want to do,
do it in those two.

33:24.919 --> 33:28.006
But then, promise me,
you'll get the divorce signed, okay?

33:30.341 --> 33:31.300
Oh.

33:33.094 --> 33:36.055
Yes. Okay. Thanks, Hyang-rae.

33:37.348 --> 33:38.433
I really just…

33:39.267 --> 33:41.436
- [Dong-han] I'll be good.
- [phone beeps]

33:45.481 --> 33:46.441
Hello?

33:48.317 --> 33:49.902
Hyang-rae, thank you!!

33:51.487 --> 33:53.239
[chuckles]

33:58.703 --> 34:00.705
[uplifting music]

34:13.259 --> 34:14.886
Now.
[hums]

34:16.137 --> 34:18.765
[exhales]
The linens are new.

34:18.848 --> 34:21.184
- They should be nice and--
- It's great. Thank you.

34:21.267 --> 34:24.270
Oh, the room's a little damp, huh?

34:24.353 --> 34:27.023
If I'd known you were staying,
I could have aired it out a little.

34:27.106 --> 34:28.983
Uh, no it's great, Mama.

34:29.067 --> 34:31.235
Should I turn the boiler on now?
Or should I wait?

34:31.319 --> 34:33.488
No, uh, we'll take care of it.

34:34.363 --> 34:36.074
- [chuckles]
- Oh, okay.

34:36.157 --> 34:37.909
Okay. Go to bed, then.

34:37.992 --> 34:39.869
- Good night.
- Good night. Good night.

34:39.952 --> 34:41.329
- Good night.
- Thank you. Thanks.

34:50.213 --> 34:51.964
[comforter rustles]

34:57.303 --> 34:59.055
I told you to go to a hotel, though.

35:00.765 --> 35:01.974
Uh…

35:02.058 --> 35:05.019
Your father told me to stay the night.
How could I say no?

35:05.686 --> 35:06.729
Not my father.

35:07.438 --> 35:09.315
Stepfathers are fathers too, Yu-jin.

35:09.398 --> 35:10.858
Don't be so harsh.

35:11.567 --> 35:14.362
- I wasn't.
- [Ki-jun] You're so cold with him.

35:14.445 --> 35:16.739
And you didn't even look at him at supper.

35:16.823 --> 35:18.616
Oppa, what do you know, huh?

35:18.699 --> 35:20.910
I'm not saying that I…

35:21.911 --> 35:24.580
He never knows where he stands with you.

35:24.664 --> 35:27.166
That's what's wrong. He's too nervous.

35:28.543 --> 35:30.336
With my mom and brother, he's so relaxed.

35:30.419 --> 35:33.965
- Well, with you, he has to--
- Yes, I know he's nice.

35:34.048 --> 35:38.094
And he's great with Mom
and a good dad for my little brother also.

35:38.177 --> 35:39.971
I don't have a home here.

35:41.430 --> 35:43.391
It's not my family now, it's theirs.

35:43.933 --> 35:46.686
That's why I wanted
to start a family of my own and yet…

35:46.769 --> 35:48.062
And yet?

35:48.146 --> 35:50.398
[breathes deeply]

35:50.481 --> 35:53.067
Forget it. Let's just sleep.

35:53.151 --> 35:56.028
You're the one who didn't want
to register our marriage.

35:57.905 --> 36:00.283
[sighs]
Do I have to remind you why?

36:00.366 --> 36:02.201
How could I trust you with that?

36:02.285 --> 36:04.579
[Yu-jin] You care more
about what people think of us,

36:04.662 --> 36:07.123
who that Jin Ha-kyung woman is dating,

36:07.206 --> 36:10.168
and how that will change whatever we have
going on in our relationship.

36:10.251 --> 36:11.419
That's because…

36:12.753 --> 36:15.047
It's because of that Lee Si-woo.

36:15.131 --> 36:17.008
[sighs]
So?

36:17.592 --> 36:19.510
Okay, fine. So what do you most hate?

36:19.594 --> 36:21.345
The fact that I lived with Si-woo?

36:21.429 --> 36:23.556
Or the fact he's dating Jin Ha-kyung?

36:24.140 --> 36:25.183
Both.

36:27.018 --> 36:28.811
Both I find very offensive.

36:28.895 --> 36:30.730
So that's why I want a conclusion.

36:30.813 --> 36:32.648
What's the conclusion, Yu-jin?

36:33.232 --> 36:35.234
You're my wife. So there.
That's our conclusion.

36:35.318 --> 36:36.694
If you regret this, let me know.

36:38.070 --> 36:39.238
We'll forget it.

36:39.989 --> 36:42.074
[gloomy music]

36:43.618 --> 36:45.244
Are you gonna keep being so mean?

36:45.870 --> 36:48.706
I got down on my knees for you.
So let's move on. Why drag it out?

36:48.789 --> 36:51.167
I'm sorry, but I couldn't live that way.

36:51.250 --> 36:54.670
Pretending we're perfect in front
of everyone like somehow you always do.

36:54.754 --> 36:56.756
Actually, all the time and lying.

36:58.049 --> 36:59.926
I can't do it that way right now.

37:00.009 --> 37:01.552
Do you think I wanna do it like that?

37:01.636 --> 37:03.304
It's just what people do.

37:03.387 --> 37:05.014
That's what married life always is.

37:05.097 --> 37:07.642
But I'm sorry I can't do that
like everyone else in the world.

37:07.725 --> 37:09.143
So then, what do we do?

37:09.227 --> 37:10.186
So let's…

37:11.270 --> 37:14.315
I don't know why you came out here
just to make me feel so awful!

37:16.525 --> 37:17.777
[door slides open]

37:17.860 --> 37:19.695
- Honey, stop it!
- What is this?

37:19.779 --> 37:21.155
Are you making my daughter cry?

37:21.239 --> 37:23.574
- Get up, you!
- Sir, no! No! That's not it!

37:23.658 --> 37:24.992
Get out. Let's get out now!

37:25.076 --> 37:26.160
- Hush.
- I…

37:27.411 --> 37:28.913
Ow, ow!
[groans]

37:30.581 --> 37:33.584
Who said you could make
my daughter cry, huh? Huh?

37:33.668 --> 37:35.211
Sir, that's not it.

37:35.294 --> 37:37.463
Honey, let go and then we'll talk, huh?

37:37.546 --> 37:40.424
I warned you once before at your wedding.

37:40.508 --> 37:44.637
I warned you that if you made
my daughter cry, you die at my hands, huh?

37:44.720 --> 37:45.721
Yeah, you said that.

37:45.805 --> 37:46.973
And then you did!

37:47.056 --> 37:49.517
You've only been married to her
for a few months!

37:49.600 --> 37:51.310
Not a decade. Not even a year.

37:51.394 --> 37:53.187
And already, you got her crying?

37:53.271 --> 37:54.647
- I should--
- Father! Don't.

37:57.024 --> 37:58.025
[Yujin's stepdad] What?

37:58.651 --> 37:59.777
"Father"?

38:01.070 --> 38:02.154
I…

38:03.572 --> 38:06.409
- Oppa, don't, huh?
- Uh…

38:09.078 --> 38:11.455
This is our problem,
and we'll be fine, sir.

38:14.208 --> 38:16.419
- Go in, oppa.
- [Ki-jun] Okay.

38:16.502 --> 38:17.503
Uh-huh.

38:17.586 --> 38:18.671
[clears throat]

38:24.302 --> 38:25.678
You heard it, right?

38:25.761 --> 38:27.847
She said father. She really said it.

38:28.389 --> 38:29.390
[chuckles]

38:30.808 --> 38:34.145
Oh, you go in too.
I'm sure they can solve it themselves.

38:34.228 --> 38:36.564
- [Yu-jin's mom] Go in.
- But I'm certain she said it.

38:36.647 --> 38:40.401
Okay. She said it. Go in.
[chuckles]

38:49.410 --> 38:50.828
[switch clicks]

38:51.829 --> 38:52.872
[door slides close]

38:52.955 --> 38:55.875
[Mi-jin] Right now, the first
and most likely scenario is

38:55.958 --> 39:00.254
it lands at Jeonnam's south coast
then crosses the Korean Peninsula,

39:00.338 --> 39:03.382
does its wrecking, then at Pohang,
it's back in the ocean.

39:04.175 --> 39:07.011
The second scenario is if it veers east.

39:07.636 --> 39:09.972
This scenario sees less total damage.

39:10.056 --> 39:11.390
However, our southern areas

39:11.474 --> 39:13.267
would have quite
severe destruction regardless.

39:13.351 --> 39:14.852
What about the third?

39:15.436 --> 39:17.521
[Mi-jin] The North Pacific high contracts.

39:17.605 --> 39:21.484
The typhoon traces the edge there,
south of Jeju Island, turning to Kyushu.

39:21.567 --> 39:25.821
In that case, I would expect it to cause
severe coastal destruction near Busan.

39:26.822 --> 39:29.742
If the high in the North Pacific
contracts just a little further,

39:29.825 --> 39:32.953
it might still veer eastward
as in scenario two, right?

39:35.164 --> 39:37.333
Looking at the current data
for the North Pacific high,

39:37.416 --> 39:38.667
I don't think that would happen.

39:39.752 --> 39:42.338
Uh, Mr. Um, is there a real likelihood

39:42.421 --> 39:44.924
of the typhoon changing course
to the south and growing weaker?

39:45.674 --> 39:48.094
Uh, it's not impossible.

39:48.177 --> 39:52.306
We can't rule out the likely chance
that it could still speed eastward

39:52.390 --> 39:53.724
because of the jet stream in the north.

39:54.892 --> 39:57.728
So it is possible that it could move
along an eastward course?

39:58.312 --> 40:00.648
[Mi-jin] Yes.
We'll need considerable ground data

40:00.731 --> 40:02.316
to get a thorough report ready for you.

40:03.317 --> 40:05.444
Could we find any more data before that?

40:07.822 --> 40:08.989
Well…

40:09.073 --> 40:11.659
[pensive music]

40:14.161 --> 40:16.163
We could launch a sonde
off the eastern side

40:16.247 --> 40:18.457
- and to the west of Jeju.
- And?

40:19.083 --> 40:20.793
Well, you know, it's far too dangerous

40:20.876 --> 40:22.920
to send anyone out in the ocean
to deploy a sonde.

40:23.003 --> 40:26.382
But it's still the best method available
to use at this moment, no?

40:29.427 --> 40:30.302
How's this, then?

40:30.803 --> 40:33.722
[Mi-jin] We'll deploy a sonde in the east
in Woljeong-ri, at least.

40:33.806 --> 40:36.851
There will be some guessing,
but it's still an improvement from now.

40:37.810 --> 40:39.228
I'll go out to sea for the west one.

40:39.311 --> 40:41.480
[tense music]

40:50.489 --> 40:51.365
[Mi-jin] Director Jin.

40:51.866 --> 40:53.659
You've never deployed a sonde, have you?

40:54.702 --> 40:55.744
And you wanna take a ship

40:55.828 --> 40:58.372
all the way out there
in this weather and do this?

40:58.956 --> 41:00.541
[Bong-chan] Director Jin. Listen to me.

41:01.876 --> 41:07.131
Sometimes, it's just not possible
to know everything all of the time.

41:07.214 --> 41:08.757
Do you understand?

41:09.508 --> 41:12.261
Typhoon number 14 was too powerful.

41:12.344 --> 41:14.597
With Elisha right at its heels,

41:14.680 --> 41:16.765
we have to assume
this could be even worse.

41:16.849 --> 41:19.727
Even if they're just predictions,
I believe it's our job to use

41:19.810 --> 41:22.813
the most accurate data
when it's available.

41:27.568 --> 41:29.653
Sir, we can't afford to fail on this.

41:32.448 --> 41:35.493
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

41:42.958 --> 41:44.335
[sighs]

41:52.009 --> 41:55.095
SEOUL, DOKDO, SEOGWIPO
OKINAWA, JAPAN

41:57.806 --> 41:59.767
[rain pouring]

42:10.986 --> 42:11.862
What is wrong?

42:11.946 --> 42:14.281
You think if you have the ship,
then you can do the sonde?

42:15.032 --> 42:18.285
In these conditions,
remote observation might not work.

42:24.208 --> 42:25.584
[sighs]

42:25.668 --> 42:27.920
[thunder roars]

42:36.470 --> 42:38.639
[waves crashing]

42:41.058 --> 42:45.229
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

42:50.985 --> 42:53.070
[ominous music]

43:38.824 --> 43:41.201
[ominous music continues]

43:42.703 --> 43:44.580
[air hisses]

43:48.292 --> 43:50.919
[thunder roars]

44:08.395 --> 44:10.439
- [radio beeps]
- Meteorology One has arrived at Ieodo.

44:11.398 --> 44:13.108
- [radio beeps]
- [Mi-jin] We're ready for you.

44:13.609 --> 44:15.569
It's going up at 21:00.

44:15.653 --> 44:16.737
- [radio beeps]
- Got it.

44:17.655 --> 44:19.948
Director, the wind's too strong after all.

44:20.032 --> 44:21.533
[Si-woo] Remote observation won't work.

44:22.117 --> 44:23.786
We'll need to do it manually.

44:23.869 --> 44:25.120
[container clacks]

44:27.414 --> 44:28.957
When we go, can you count down?

44:29.041 --> 44:30.250
Mm-hmm, okay.

44:34.296 --> 44:36.757
[tense music]

45:05.411 --> 45:07.329
Five, four…

45:07.413 --> 45:08.956
[Ha-kyung shouting]
Three…

45:09.540 --> 45:11.542
two, one!

45:12.084 --> 45:13.293
[clinks]

45:34.148 --> 45:37.317
[thunder roaring]

45:37.985 --> 45:40.487
- [machine beeping]
- [Bong-chan sighs]

45:50.497 --> 45:52.416
[anxious exhale]

45:54.501 --> 45:57.171
[thrilling music]

46:14.438 --> 46:16.023
[beeping]

46:18.150 --> 46:20.319
[machine beeping]

46:20.402 --> 46:22.988
[continuous trilling]

46:23.071 --> 46:24.907
We got it. It's reporting now.

46:26.200 --> 46:27.367
[sighs]

46:27.993 --> 46:30.579
[trilling]

46:30.662 --> 46:31.955
[beeps]

46:38.754 --> 46:39.588
Okay.

46:39.671 --> 46:41.256
[Seok-ho] We're getting data from Ieodo.

46:41.340 --> 46:42.925
[Dong-han] Oh, really?

46:43.008 --> 46:44.092
[Bong-chan relieved sigh]

46:45.010 --> 46:47.304
[keyboard clacking]

46:49.681 --> 46:50.766
Oh…

46:53.435 --> 46:55.187
Did you see what's coming through?

46:55.270 --> 46:56.813
Yes, we're adding it to the array now.

46:56.897 --> 46:58.398
First, we just need to check the NWP.

46:58.482 --> 47:00.984
[Ha-kyung] Send me the data
from the model as soon as it's done.

47:01.068 --> 47:03.028
- [Dong-han] Okay.
- [phone beeps]

47:03.111 --> 47:04.738
TYPHOON TRACK PREDICTION

47:07.616 --> 47:09.284
Well, I think what you said was true.

47:09.368 --> 47:11.870
If it stays on track,
it will move along Namhae,

47:11.954 --> 47:14.122
and the damages
should be limited to the south.

47:16.291 --> 47:18.961
[pensive music]

47:20.796 --> 47:23.423
- [radio beeps]
- Did you get the NWP?

47:23.507 --> 47:24.716
Yes, I've got it right now.

47:25.217 --> 47:27.344
Looks like Namhae is where it's headed.

47:27.928 --> 47:28.929
It isn't.

47:29.846 --> 47:30.806
[radio beeps]

47:30.889 --> 47:32.933
- What?
- [Ha-kyung] That's the data.

47:33.016 --> 47:35.269
But let's just publish the first scenario.

47:35.852 --> 47:37.521
- [Mi-jin] Are you serious?
- [radio beeps]

47:37.604 --> 47:38.897
Yes.

47:38.981 --> 47:41.358
I checked
with Director General Ko already.

47:43.235 --> 47:46.697
Director Jin. You know we're going
to be disciplined for this, don't you?

47:47.489 --> 47:51.034
- [radio beeps]
- I'm aware. I'll bear the consequence.

47:51.118 --> 47:54.246
- [radio beeps]
- Why would you ever take such a risk?

47:54.329 --> 47:56.415
If the typhoon diverges
from what we publish,

47:56.498 --> 47:59.293
only I'll take the blame, okay?
It's my department.

48:01.545 --> 48:03.088
- [radio beeps]
- So can we release?

48:10.178 --> 48:12.889
Okay. We'll publish scenario one.

48:14.182 --> 48:16.268
Good work, Director Jin Ha-kyung.

48:16.351 --> 48:17.311
You as well.

48:19.646 --> 48:22.524
[feel-good music]

48:26.695 --> 48:29.573
PRESS RELEASE

48:31.617 --> 48:32.451
Huh?

48:33.035 --> 48:34.286
We're exaggerating?

48:35.412 --> 48:36.622
Yeah.

48:36.705 --> 48:39.416
Director Jin said we're going
with scenario one.

48:40.000 --> 48:43.420
I want to stay prepared for the chance
that the northern jet stream

48:43.503 --> 48:44.755
is weaker than we thought,

48:44.838 --> 48:47.841
and the typhoon starts
to head farther to the west.

48:47.924 --> 48:50.427
[sucks teeth]
Still, it's very alarmist, no?

48:50.510 --> 48:52.054
The point of the forecast

48:52.137 --> 48:55.182
is to protect our country
and the people living here.

48:55.265 --> 48:57.934
[Ha-kyung] Not to be perfectly accurate.
That's what I was taught.

48:59.311 --> 49:01.146
All right, Director Jin.

49:01.229 --> 49:04.066
Scenario one's going down the hall
to the press.

49:05.734 --> 49:07.903
- [phone beeps]
- [chuckles]

49:07.986 --> 49:10.322
TYPHOON ELISHA HEADING NORTH
TO THE SOUTHERN SEA OF JEJU

49:10.405 --> 49:12.658
EXPECTED TO HIT
THE SOUTHERN COAST AT DAWN

49:12.741 --> 49:14.660
- [door lock beeps]
- News.

49:15.786 --> 49:17.162
News.
[sighs]

49:20.248 --> 49:22.417
- [TV turns on]
- News.

49:23.377 --> 49:24.461
[news anchor] Breaking news.

49:24.544 --> 49:28.256
Typhoon No. 15 known as Elisha
is no longer expected to track north,

49:28.340 --> 49:29.758
but instead cross Korea,

49:29.841 --> 49:32.761
making landfall south of Jeonnam
early tomorrow morning.

49:32.844 --> 49:34.096
Elisha is a strong storm

49:34.179 --> 49:36.473
with a central wind speed
of 30m per second.

49:37.224 --> 49:39.685
According to the KMA,
Elisha will be of a similar severity

49:39.768 --> 49:41.311
- as Ricky which preceded it.
- Bo-mi.

49:41.395 --> 49:43.313
You ran home to watch the weather?

49:43.397 --> 49:45.065
- However, its center will pass…
- Yeah.

49:45.148 --> 49:46.650
Dad did this one.

49:46.733 --> 49:48.819
[news anchor] So it is expected
to have a stronger impact.

49:48.902 --> 49:51.655
When did you get so interested
in your father's work?

49:51.738 --> 49:54.324
[news anchor] …also added that citizens
should take special care

49:54.408 --> 49:56.868
against strong winds
and rain throughout the night.

49:59.496 --> 50:00.497
- Mr. Shin.
- [Seok-ho] Yes, sir?

50:00.580 --> 50:01.998
[Dong-han] Take these stats to AD Oh.

50:02.082 --> 50:04.334
- And give me the situation data.
- [Seok-ho] Okay.

50:06.753 --> 50:09.464
[Myung-ju] Soo-jin, here,
typhoon information.

50:09.548 --> 50:11.758
- Oh, okay. Uh-huh.
- Can you deliver it? Thank you.

50:11.842 --> 50:12.801
[sighs]

50:16.012 --> 50:18.682
- So from here…
- Yes, like this.

50:18.765 --> 50:20.016
[Seok-ho] Yeah, that's it.

50:21.977 --> 50:24.312
[gentle music]

50:27.607 --> 50:29.067
[sighs]
Okay, that's done.

50:29.985 --> 50:32.863
So we're really going
with scenario one, huh?

50:33.864 --> 50:34.906
[Ha-kyung] Mm-hmm.

50:36.533 --> 50:38.910
[waves crashing]

50:39.745 --> 50:41.872
- [gasps]
- [ship creaking]

50:45.500 --> 50:47.544
[romantic music]

50:52.674 --> 50:54.843
[Ha-kyung] Now, it's my turn.

50:56.261 --> 51:00.599
Which scenario do I choose
in this breakup with you?

51:02.267 --> 51:05.020
Scenario one. Cling to him.

51:08.690 --> 51:09.900
Scenario two.

51:10.400 --> 51:12.569
Accept the breakup without a fuss.

51:15.238 --> 51:16.406
Scenario three.

51:17.324 --> 51:21.286
Drag it out and try to get some more time.

51:29.377 --> 51:31.838
So what is it you want?

51:36.176 --> 51:38.553
[romantic music]

51:39.346 --> 51:41.223
Give me a little longer.

51:57.739 --> 51:59.741
[rain pattering]

52:07.749 --> 52:08.834
What is it?

52:09.626 --> 52:11.878
Did something go wrong at work?

52:13.505 --> 52:14.714
I don't think…

52:17.008 --> 52:18.260
I can't do this.

52:19.594 --> 52:20.637
Do what?

52:20.720 --> 52:22.639
I can't see you, Tae-kyung.

52:23.932 --> 52:27.894
I have trouble trying to focus
on more than one thing.

52:28.603 --> 52:29.813
Okay, so?

52:30.397 --> 52:31.231
Ever…

52:31.815 --> 52:33.984
since the first time that I met you,

52:34.693 --> 52:37.737
my priorities have been all turned around.

52:37.821 --> 52:38.822
But…

52:39.406 --> 52:41.408
At the KMA, you won't survive like that.

52:41.491 --> 52:43.910
What was your first priority?

52:44.661 --> 52:46.496
The office, of course, the weather.

52:47.038 --> 52:49.499
So what about now?

52:55.088 --> 52:57.340
["Melting" by CHEEZE playing]

53:00.135 --> 53:00.969
Oh?

53:02.387 --> 53:03.805
[sighs]

53:04.723 --> 53:05.932
[Seok-ho] I…

53:06.975 --> 53:09.311
I'm really not like this at all.

53:09.394 --> 53:10.353
Okay?

53:10.437 --> 53:14.900
I'm… I always have this line
between home and when I go to work.

53:14.983 --> 53:17.277
And I've never once crossed it, okay?

53:17.944 --> 53:21.239
I'm logical and rational, but still, I…

53:21.323 --> 53:22.449
Still, you…

53:24.409 --> 53:26.119
I feel confused and I don't…

53:27.412 --> 53:28.580
[exhales deeply]

53:28.663 --> 53:30.457
I don't know what to do
with all of these feelings.

53:30.540 --> 53:32.125
I can't control and can't shut out.

53:32.626 --> 53:35.462
And if I keep going and make an error,
the citizens will suffer and I'll…

53:35.545 --> 53:38.006
I won't ever forgive myself.
I'll hate myself for it.

53:38.089 --> 53:40.008
And get all swept up in regret and misery.

53:40.091 --> 53:42.552
- And then I'll--
- Shin Seok-ho!

53:42.636 --> 53:43.678
Yes?

53:52.103 --> 53:53.104
[lips smack]

53:54.814 --> 53:55.649
Oh!

53:56.274 --> 53:58.735
["Melting" by CHEEZE playing]

54:01.529 --> 54:03.782
[anxious exhale]
I also like you!

54:05.450 --> 54:06.910
[chuckles]

54:07.619 --> 54:08.703
Oh, really?

54:09.204 --> 54:10.997
[giggles]

54:11.915 --> 54:13.625
You haven't had dinner yet, right?

54:14.125 --> 54:16.127
Let's do mung bean pancakes
with rice wine.

54:16.211 --> 54:17.587
[Tae-kyung] Let's go.
Has the rain stopped?

54:23.927 --> 54:25.553
Wait. Don't leave yet. I…

54:31.434 --> 54:32.602
[Seok-ho] I'm coming!

54:34.896 --> 54:37.065
["Melting" by CHEEZE playing]

54:50.870 --> 54:54.165
[clock ticking]

54:55.500 --> 54:56.418
[clonks]

54:56.501 --> 54:58.169
- [friend 1] Yeah!
- Oh, yeah!

54:58.253 --> 55:00.338
If only I can fix my life
with a swing, huh?

55:00.422 --> 55:02.173
Yeah, you're on a roll today.
You're crazy.

55:02.257 --> 55:03.091
[cheers]

55:03.174 --> 55:04.300
[laughter]

55:05.468 --> 55:07.095
- Yeah!
- [all laughing]

55:08.430 --> 55:11.099
- [clacks]
- [friends cheering]

55:11.182 --> 55:13.226
- Yeah, another one, huh?
- [friend 1] Yeah, sure.

55:14.144 --> 55:15.478
- Here, right? I get a point.
- Oh, yeah!

55:15.562 --> 55:17.313
- One more, huh? Another?
- [friend 2] Oh, yeah!

55:17.397 --> 55:19.065
[chuckling]

55:24.529 --> 55:25.739
How come you're out here?

55:27.240 --> 55:28.867
What are you doing here, Myung-ju?

55:29.451 --> 55:31.369
See? I told you I saw Dad go out.

55:31.453 --> 55:33.663
I said he went down to the batting cages.

55:33.747 --> 55:35.874
Yesterday and the day before that too.

55:35.957 --> 55:38.001
Right, Dad? Did I get it right?

55:38.960 --> 55:40.211
[Chan-yi giggles]

55:46.092 --> 55:48.178
[somber music]

55:50.346 --> 55:53.308
- [can clanks]
- [Myung-ju breathes deeply]

55:55.393 --> 55:57.854
You have, um, three scenarios.

55:59.272 --> 56:00.356
"Scenarios"?

56:00.940 --> 56:01.900
Number one.

56:02.525 --> 56:03.693
Get your old job again.

56:04.319 --> 56:06.112
- Honey.
- Two.

56:06.905 --> 56:08.198
I divorce you.

56:09.324 --> 56:10.825
- Honey!
- [Myung-ju] Three.

56:11.618 --> 56:13.203
You're gonna study your ass off.

56:19.375 --> 56:20.543
[Myung-ju sighs]

56:20.627 --> 56:23.880
Do you think I'm running this family
because I have an abundance of energy?

56:23.963 --> 56:27.217
It's because you've got this dream,
and even now, at our age,

56:27.300 --> 56:29.385
I wanted you to try it
before time ran out.

56:30.011 --> 56:31.888
So you wouldn't live with regrets.

56:31.971 --> 56:34.599
It's so difficult. I'm so tired.

56:35.433 --> 56:37.143
But I thought this was the only shot.

56:37.644 --> 56:39.479
So I said that you should give it a try.

56:40.605 --> 56:41.564
And now what?

56:42.774 --> 56:44.109
You're too stressed?

56:47.529 --> 56:48.905
[sighs]

56:51.741 --> 56:55.203
Aren't you the slightest bit ashamed
about all of it, giving me your lies

56:55.286 --> 56:57.038
and ignoring our kids?

57:05.171 --> 57:07.215
And what about your mother, then, huh?

57:07.298 --> 57:10.051
She used to watch our two little boys
every day of the month.

57:15.932 --> 57:16.808
Myung-ju.

57:17.809 --> 57:18.852
I'm very sorry.

57:20.145 --> 57:21.354
I was terrible.

57:21.438 --> 57:22.522
[sobs]

57:25.775 --> 57:26.693
Choose, then.

57:28.069 --> 57:30.864
Scenario one, two, or three?

57:34.284 --> 57:35.743
[sighs]

57:36.995 --> 57:39.122
[birds chirping]

57:40.206 --> 57:43.376
What is happening? Why is there sun?

57:43.460 --> 57:46.379
[reporter] Typhoon number 15, Elisha,
which was expected to hit the country

57:46.463 --> 57:47.714
early this morning.

57:47.797 --> 57:50.258
- It crossed the South Sea at four…
- Bo-mi, have you been here all night?

57:50.341 --> 57:51.551
[reporter] …in the morning
in the eastern seas…

57:51.634 --> 57:55.513
- I'm so… annoyed.
- What? Why?

57:55.597 --> 57:56.431
The news.

57:56.514 --> 57:57.974
[reporter] …extra tropical cyclones

57:58.057 --> 57:59.559
and eventually fade away.

58:00.351 --> 58:04.981
Unlike the forecast from the KMA
which showed the typhoon battering Korea…

58:05.064 --> 58:07.484
- …it passed by without incidents.
- Oh, the forecast?

58:07.567 --> 58:11.946
Why did he get it wrong?
He was spot on with Number 14.

58:12.530 --> 58:14.491
Getting it perfect isn't the point.

58:14.574 --> 58:17.744
The typhoon passed with barely any damage,
that's what counts.

58:18.620 --> 58:20.622
[light music]

58:21.581 --> 58:22.415
What?

58:23.374 --> 58:24.584
Goosebumps.

58:25.585 --> 58:26.794
[Bo-mi] What was that, Mom?

58:26.878 --> 58:30.673
I thought there is nothing between you
since you were apart for so long.

58:31.257 --> 58:32.383
And?

58:32.467 --> 58:34.344
You sounded just like a KMA employee.

58:34.427 --> 58:35.678
[scoffs]

58:35.762 --> 58:38.097
That's ridiculous.
Go and get ready for school.

58:38.181 --> 58:39.557
We'll have breakfast in a minute.

58:39.641 --> 58:41.976
- [door lock beeps]
- [door opens]

58:42.060 --> 58:43.353
[Dong-han sighs]

58:43.436 --> 58:44.854
- Honey.
- [door closes]

58:45.897 --> 58:46.773
[Dong-han] Bo-mi.

58:47.357 --> 58:48.733
I brought hangover soup for us.

58:49.442 --> 58:50.777
Hangover soup?

58:50.860 --> 58:51.945
What?

58:52.028 --> 58:53.780
You used to love this
when you were little.

58:55.490 --> 58:56.866
That was a long time ago.

58:56.950 --> 58:59.369
I know. And that place is actually
still selling the same soup.

58:59.953 --> 59:02.497
There were tons of people there.
You haven't had breakfast, huh?

59:02.580 --> 59:05.166
You don't need to heat anything up.
We can eat now. Come on.

59:07.627 --> 59:11.172
[Dong-han] I asked them
for a lot of blood pudding.

59:12.757 --> 59:13.800
'Cause it's so great.

59:13.883 --> 59:16.427
[chuckles]
It smells good.

59:17.136 --> 59:19.847
Right? Uh, bowls?

59:19.931 --> 59:21.307
- [Bo-mi] Here.
- [Dong-han] Oh, thanks.

59:22.100 --> 59:23.518
Some spoons also. Yeah.

59:26.479 --> 59:27.730
[Dong-han] See this?

59:27.814 --> 59:29.107
[plastic crinkles]

59:29.190 --> 59:30.358
[Bo-mi] Too small?

59:31.651 --> 59:33.861
Huh? No, just eat.

59:33.945 --> 59:36.489
- [Dong-han] Wait, we need spoons.
- [Bo-mi] Here.

59:43.621 --> 59:45.873
[playful music]

01:00:03.141 --> 01:00:04.225
[Soo-ja] Huh?

01:00:19.407 --> 01:00:21.075
[gasps]

01:00:24.495 --> 01:00:26.372
Well, what do you know.

01:00:39.260 --> 01:00:40.386
[Si-woo] Put this on.

01:00:55.318 --> 01:00:56.486
So how is your eye?

01:01:01.491 --> 01:01:02.742
[Si-woo] It feels fine.

01:01:03.368 --> 01:01:05.620
You didn't have to follow me out to sea.

01:01:08.665 --> 01:01:09.582
I told you.

01:01:09.666 --> 01:01:12.210
It's very technical, sending up a sonde.

01:01:15.171 --> 01:01:16.339
And I also…

01:01:17.090 --> 01:01:18.758
agreed with what you said earlier

01:01:19.509 --> 01:01:23.513
about Elisha heading to the east
instead of across Korea.

01:01:27.183 --> 01:01:29.060
I came because I wanted to check it out.

01:01:29.602 --> 01:01:31.104
That's the only reason.

01:01:35.650 --> 01:01:37.110
You'll do okay on your own?

01:01:40.822 --> 01:01:44.492
Do you think we can work together
even after it's over?

01:01:47.370 --> 01:01:50.456
Are you gonna be okay on your own?

01:01:52.709 --> 01:01:54.711
["Love Hurts A Little More"
by Kim Na-young playing]

01:02:02.719 --> 01:02:04.011
Yeah, I think so.

01:02:06.139 --> 01:02:07.390
[Ha-kyung] I'll be fine.

01:02:11.519 --> 01:02:12.895
Let's just end it.

01:02:19.610 --> 01:02:21.237
We're over now, Si-woo.

01:02:35.543 --> 01:02:36.586
Okay, sure.

01:02:48.598 --> 01:02:53.186
[Ha-kyung] Typhoons happen
to release the thermal imbalance

01:02:53.269 --> 01:02:54.687
from the Earth's rotation.

01:02:58.733 --> 01:03:02.779
Unlike the typhoon forecast
that the authorities gave us earlier,

01:03:02.862 --> 01:03:04.655
it was a non-existent storm.

01:03:04.739 --> 01:03:07.408
- [reporter] Polls are showing…
- Yes, I'm sorry. Yes.

01:03:07.492 --> 01:03:10.995
- [reporter] …lowers faith in the KMA.
- Ah, yes. Yes, I see it. Yes.

01:03:11.579 --> 01:03:12.914
KMA'S TYPHOON MIS-FORECAST

01:03:12.997 --> 01:03:14.123
SHAMEFUL TYPHOON WARNING

01:03:14.207 --> 01:03:15.041
[Bong-chan] Well…

01:03:15.124 --> 01:03:17.084
YOU SAID THE TYPHOON WAS COMING!
WHERE IS ELISHA?

01:03:19.879 --> 01:03:20.755
Yes.

01:03:21.756 --> 01:03:24.717
Yes. I will report right back.

01:03:29.305 --> 01:03:31.641
[groans, inhales]

01:03:34.727 --> 01:03:36.979
STOP EXCESSIVE FORECASTS.
WE WANT AN ACCURATE WEATHER REPORT.

01:03:37.980 --> 01:03:41.776
[Ha-kyung] The typhoon might
make this harder for us now, but…

01:03:50.952 --> 01:03:55.957
in the long run, it's good as it renews
the water for our environment.

01:03:56.040 --> 01:03:58.042
["Love Hurts A Little More"
by Kim Na-young playing]

01:04:10.263 --> 01:04:12.223
[breathes deeply]

01:04:16.644 --> 01:04:17.728
As long…

01:04:19.230 --> 01:04:22.149
as we can just survive that moment.

01:04:25.152 --> 01:04:28.239
DOMESTIC FLIGHTS

01:04:43.337 --> 01:04:44.630
I'll see you at the office.

01:04:48.759 --> 01:04:50.052
Should I bring your stuff to you?

01:04:51.220 --> 01:04:52.179
I'll…

01:04:52.263 --> 01:04:54.223
come get them on my next weekend.

01:04:56.183 --> 01:04:57.143
Sounds good.

01:04:58.769 --> 01:04:59.812
Okay.

01:05:07.028 --> 01:05:09.280
["Love Hurts A Little More"
by Kim Na-young playing]

01:05:34.513 --> 01:05:37.350
Why so nervous? I mean, it's our house.

01:05:47.318 --> 01:05:48.361
Come on.

01:05:56.869 --> 01:05:57.870
[grunts]

01:06:08.923 --> 01:06:13.386
LIQUID IRON SUPPLEMENT FOR PREGNANT WOMEN

01:06:13.469 --> 01:06:16.055
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:06:18.557 --> 01:06:21.018
- [staff] Have a good meal.
- Oh. Thanks, you too.

01:06:25.940 --> 01:06:27.149
Si-woo.

01:06:28.693 --> 01:06:30.111
Oh, yeah.

01:06:30.194 --> 01:06:32.363
[chuckling]

01:06:33.864 --> 01:06:36.492
Well, I heard
that you're dating Director Jin.

01:06:37.743 --> 01:06:38.744
What?

01:06:38.828 --> 01:06:41.330
I feel so bad, so sorry.

01:06:41.414 --> 01:06:44.917
I must have gotten in the way
when we both stayed over with her.

01:06:45.001 --> 01:06:46.961
So when did it start? While we were there?

01:06:48.546 --> 01:06:51.507
Uh, wait, no, uh…
Who did you hear that from?

01:06:51.590 --> 01:06:53.217
[Dong-han] Nobody, really.

01:06:53.300 --> 01:06:55.678
Everyone on the team knew. I was the last.

01:06:56.679 --> 01:06:58.389
Everyone… How?

01:06:58.472 --> 01:06:59.765
I don't know.

01:07:00.349 --> 01:07:02.685
[Dong-han] You know,
you're pretty brave, aren't you?

01:07:02.768 --> 01:07:07.732
Of all people, our director
while we all work together, man. Gosh!

01:07:07.815 --> 01:07:09.692
[woman]
Forecaster Lee is dating Director Jin.

01:07:09.775 --> 01:07:11.819
But no, for real, though.

01:07:12.695 --> 01:07:14.572
Good for the two of you.

01:07:15.281 --> 01:07:18.117
[Dong-han] You guys
are great together. Congratulations!

01:07:18.200 --> 01:07:21.245
I'm serious. I was just teasing.

01:07:21.328 --> 01:07:23.164
And I am sorry.

01:07:23.247 --> 01:07:25.583
I was so oblivious, wasn't I, huh?

01:07:25.666 --> 01:07:28.377
[woman 1 whispering]
Is he dating Director Jin?

01:07:28.461 --> 01:07:31.464
- [woman 2] Oh, good for them.
- [man 3] Yeah.

01:07:31.547 --> 01:07:33.049
[people murmuring]

01:07:33.132 --> 01:07:34.633
[Dong-han] Congratulations!

01:07:34.717 --> 01:07:37.470
[water running]

01:07:38.471 --> 01:07:39.722
[door opens]

01:07:41.348 --> 01:07:44.185
[squeaking]

01:07:52.401 --> 01:07:54.487
[door lock beeping]

01:07:57.406 --> 01:07:58.783
[panting]

01:07:58.866 --> 01:08:01.118
Director! Director!

01:08:03.788 --> 01:08:05.331
[panting]

01:08:11.879 --> 01:08:13.089
Are you here for your stuff?

01:08:13.172 --> 01:08:15.257
I told you I'd bring it to you. Hang on.

01:08:15.341 --> 01:08:16.550
Hey, something's wrong.

01:08:17.802 --> 01:08:18.719
What?

01:08:18.803 --> 01:08:20.596
They found out about the two of us.

01:08:21.680 --> 01:08:22.765
Wha… what?

01:08:22.848 --> 01:08:24.475
That we've been together.

01:08:25.392 --> 01:08:26.227
Huh?

01:08:26.310 --> 01:08:28.437
That I was dating you!

01:08:28.521 --> 01:08:31.065
Everybody knows about what went on
between the two of us.

01:08:31.148 --> 01:08:32.358
- What?
- [door opens]

01:08:32.942 --> 01:08:33.984
Mom!

01:08:38.364 --> 01:08:41.283
I just knew. I knew.

01:08:41.909 --> 01:08:45.037
So you two had a little office romance,

01:08:45.121 --> 01:08:46.038
- didn't you?
- Mom, no, I--

01:08:46.122 --> 01:08:49.291
Oh, I really just knew
something was going on.

01:08:50.626 --> 01:08:52.962
- No way! We're not--
- [Soo-ja] Not what, huh?

01:08:56.674 --> 01:08:58.968
And I also knew that you would deny it.

01:08:59.051 --> 01:09:01.887
So I brought my undeniable proof.

01:09:09.019 --> 01:09:10.479
[Soo-ja] Take a good look.

01:09:10.563 --> 01:09:11.939
Still deny it?

01:09:18.988 --> 01:09:21.115
[upbeat music]

01:09:59.820 --> 01:10:02.781
[Si-woo] People are taking it
more seriously than they should.

01:10:03.699 --> 01:10:06.577
[Ha-kyung] Ignore them.
Don't listen to them or reply.

01:10:06.660 --> 01:10:08.913
But I made dumpling soup, your favorite.

01:10:08.996 --> 01:10:10.497
I just have a stomachache.

01:10:10.581 --> 01:10:13.709
I thought he'd be much more mature.
But he turned out to be a baby.

01:10:13.792 --> 01:10:15.211
You must really love him.

01:10:15.878 --> 01:10:17.296
[Si-woo] We broke up.

01:10:17.880 --> 01:10:20.299
You can't maintain
a relationship if it's one-sided.

01:10:20.382 --> 01:10:23.010
- Hey! Where should we go?
- [sighs]

01:10:23.093 --> 01:10:24.762
[Ha-kyung] I have something to tell you.

01:10:24.845 --> 01:10:28.057
To be honest, Forecaster Lee and I…
